e frequent foreground color forms long 8-connected contour fragments.\n  66:     - The other foreground color is a fixed distractor/obstacle color that partitions\n  67:       the background but is never recolored.\n  68: \n  69:     Rule:\n  70:     - Split the background into 4-connected regions using all foreground pixels as\n  71:       barriers.\n  72:     - Keep the two largest background regions as the outside of the contour drawing.\n  73:     - Recolor every other background region that touches a long contour component\n  74:       to the contour color; leave all foreground pixels unchanged.\n  75: \n  76:     Key insight:\n  77:     The apparent area fill is exactly a component-level fill of bounded background\n  78:     compartments, not a row-wise interpolation between individual contour pixels.\n  79:     \"\"\"\n  80:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)\n  81:     bg = get_bg(g)\n  82:     foreground = colors_present(g, exclude={bg})\n  83:     assert len(foreground) == 2, \"expected exactly two foreground colors\"\n  84: \n  85:     fill_color = _unique_largest_color(g, foreground)\n  86:     fill_lab, _n_fill = label_mask(g == fill_color, connectivity=8)\n  87:     long_ids = _long_component_ids(fill_lab, _n_fill)\n  88: \n  89:     bg_lab, n_bg = label_mask(g == bg, connectivity=4)\n  90:     exterior_ids = _two_exterior_bg_ids(bg_lab, n_bg)\n  91: \n  92:     out = g.copy()\n  93:     for comp_id in range(1, n_bg + 1):\n  94:         if comp_id in exterior_ids:\n  95:             continue\n  96:         coords = np.argwhere(bg_lab == comp_id)\n  97:         if _touches_long_contour(coords, fill_lab, long_ids):\n  98:             out[bg_lab == comp_id] = fill_color\n  99: \n 100:     return out\n 101: \n 102: # --------------- generator (att2) ---------------\n 103: \n 104: # Canvas and palette.\n 105: H, W = 30, 30\n 106: GRID_SHAPE = (H, W)\n 107: ARC_COLOR_COUNT = 10\n 108: \n 109: # Long contour path layout.\n 110: PATH_COUNT_OPTIONS = (2, 3)\n 