{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/eval_new/seed720058768/4/codegen_prompts/3.md\"","aggregated_output":"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/4`\n- 题号：`3`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/eval_new/seed720058768/4/3.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"3\">\n- `description`：将网格中的\"种子像素\"按其所在区域的边框形状进行克隆扩展，再根据区域间的箭头指向传播颜色替换。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景色（bg）为黑色。\n  - 网格中有若干个用灰色像素画出的封闭矩形边框（各边框大小可能不同，但内部至少 3x3）。边框之间不重叠、不相邻。\n  - 每个矩形边框内部恰好有一个彩色\"种子像素\"（非黑、非灰），位于边框内某个位置。不同边框内的种子像素颜色各不相同。\n  - 部分矩形边框的某一条边上有一个 1 像素的缺口（灰色像素被替换为黑色背景），缺口位置在该边的中点处。\n  - 从一个边框的缺口向外延伸，有一条由该边框内种子颜色构成的 1 像素宽\"箭头线段\"，长度为 2-4 格，指向另一个边框的外壁（箭头线段的末端紧邻目标边框的灰色外壁）。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 第一步——种子扩展：在每个矩形边框内部，将种子像素的颜色按照\"十字扩展\"方式填充——从种子位置向上、下、左、右四个方向延伸，直到碰到灰色边框壁为止，形成一个十字形的彩色图案（种子本身位于十字中心）。\n  - 第二步——颜色传播：找到所有箭头线段。每条箭头线段从源边框的缺口出发，指向目标边框。将目标边框内已经扩展好的十字图案的颜色全部替换为源边框的种子颜色（即源边框的颜色\"入侵\"了目标边框）。\n  - 若存在链式传播（A 指向 B，B 指向 C），则按箭头方向依次执行：先处理没有入箭头的源头边框，再沿链传播。\n  - 箭头线段本身在输出中保留不变。灰色边框和缺口保持不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要先独立发现\"种子在边框内十字扩展\"的局部规则，再发现\"箭头线段传递颜色替换\"的全局传播规则。两层规则缺一不可：仅看单个边框能发现扩展，但颜色替换必须通过比较有箭头连接和无箭头连接的边框才能归纳出来。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：eval/8b7bacbf, train/465b7d93, eval/dbff022c, train/db7260a4, train/753ea09b, train/8a6d367c, train/5adee1b2, eval/581f7754\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"8b7bacbf\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3561\nmechanism=0.4024\nlexical=0.0123\ncode_feature=0.6667\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:counter, object:closed_region, object:frame, object:hole, object:marker, operation:count, operation:flood_fill, relation:adjacent, relation:inside\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/8b7bacbf.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/8b7bacbf.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nFill enclosed regions along a line seeded by unique border pixels.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.\n- Colored lines/drawings on the grid.\n- Unique single-pixel colors on the grid border mark seed endpoints of each line.\n\nRule:\n- Each border seed pixel connects (8-connected) to a line drawing.\n- Find closed bg cavities whose boundary touches that line.\n- Flood-fill each such cavity with the seed pixel's color.\n\nKey insight: Only cavities reachable through the seed's own line get filled; the seed's unique color acts as a per-line fill label.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"summary\": \"Find single pixels on grid edges that are endpoints of lines, trace along the line to find connected closed regions, and fill those regions with the edge pixel's color.\",\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"single colored pixels s on grid edge that are endpoints of a line\",\n  \"dst\": \"closed regions d connected to the line\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"d is reachable by following the line from s\",\n  \"path\": \"trace along the continuous line from edge pixel s\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"fill interior of each closed region d encountered along path with s.color\",\n  \"transform\": \"d.interior.color = s.color\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": null,\n  \"multi_step\": \"Step 1: identify single pixels on grid edge; Step 2: trace the line connected to each edge pixel; Step 3: for each closed region touching the line, flood-fill its interior with edge pixel color\",\n  \"concepts\": [\n    \"flood-fill\",\n    \"path-tracing\",\n    \"edge-detection\",\n    \"region-filling\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"465b7d93\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3361\nmechanism=0.4156\nlexical=0.0102\ncode_feature=0.4286\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, object:closed_region, object:frame, object:line_segment, object:rectangle, object:sprite, relation:adjacent, relation:between, relation:inside, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/465b7d93.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/465b7d93.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nMove the small colored sprite into the hollow frame by stretching its shape to the frame interior.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- There are exactly two foreground colors: one forms a complete rectangular\n  one-pixel-thick frame, and the other forms one 4-connected sprite outside it.\n- The frame interior is initially background.\n\nRule:\n- Clear the original sprite from its outside location.\n- Map the sprite bbox to the frame interior bbox, sending bbox extremes to\n  interior extremes.\n- Draw straight horizontal or vertical segments between mapped positions of\n  adjacent sprite pixels, then fill any enclosed background region inside\n  those drawn segments.\n\nKey insight:\nThe outside sprite is a miniature line/fill diagram for the frame interior,\nnot a bitmap to scale by block replication.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"small colored sprite s outside the frame\",\n  \"dst\": \"hollow rectangular frame interior d\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"unique s maps to unique d; s.bbox extremes align to d.bbox extremes\",\n  \"transform\": \"clear s; stretch s into d by mapping bbox extremes, drawing 4-adjacent segments, and filling enclosed regions\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"dbff022c\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3392\nmechanism=0.4071\nlexical=0.0119\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, object:closed_region, object:frame, object:hole, object:sprite, operation:flood_fill, relation:adjacent, relation:direction, relation:inside, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/dbff022c.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/dbff022c.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nFill hollow sprites' interiors using a color-palette legend on the grid edge.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color. Several hollow sprites with distinct border colors.\n- A small 2×N or N×2 palette block sits on one grid edge; one row/column lists border colors, the other lists corresponding fill colors.\n\nRule:\n- Locate the palette legend on a grid edge and read it as a border→fill color mapping.\n- Find enclosed bg regions (holes) inside sprites that don't touch the grid boundary.\n- For each hole, identify the most common adjacent border color, look it up in the palette, and fill the hole with the mapped fill color.\n\nKey insight: The palette's edge position and orientation determine reading direction; border colors in the palette uniquely key into fill colors.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"summary\": \"Use a color palette legend on the grid edge to fill sprites' interiors based on their border color mapping.\",\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"hollow sprites with colored borders s\",\n  \"dst\": \"interior of same sprite d\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"d.fill_color == palette_lookup(s.border_color)\",\n  \"path\": \"\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"\",\n  \"transform\": \"fill d with palette[s.border_color]\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": \"palette is 2xN or Nx2 block on grid edge; read direction based on edge position: top edge reads top-to-bottom, bottom edge reads bottom-to-top, left edge reads left-to-right; first row/column is border color, second is fill color\",\n  \"multi_step\": \"Step 1: locate 2xN or Nx2 palette legend on grid edge; Step 2: build color mapping (border -> fill) based on reading direction; Step 3: for each hollow sprite, lookup border color in palette and fill interior with corresponding fill color\",\n  \"concepts\": [\n    \"color-mapping\",\n    \"lookup-table\",\n    \"flood-fill\",\n    \"border-detection\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"The challenge is correctly reading the palette legend based on its edge position and orientation\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"db7260a4\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3143\nmechanism=0.4004\nlexical=0.0101\ncode_feature=0.3333\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:hole, object:line_segment, object:marker, object:rectangle, object:sprite, output:same_size, relation:between, relation:direction, relation:inside, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/db7260a4.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/db7260a4.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nDrop the singleton marker into the matching red U-shaped container, or make a bottom-row puddle if no closed container is hit.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid has a dominant background, one singleton marker pixel on the top row,\n  and one other foreground color forming vertical bars and bottom segments.\n- A closed container is a U shape: two vertical side bars with a continuous\n  bottom segment between them and an empty rectangular interior above the bottom.\n\nRule\n- Remove the top marker from its original cell.\n- If exactly one closed U-shaped container has the marker column within its\n  horizontal footprint, fill that container's empty interior with the marker color.\n- If no closed container is under the marker column, fill the whole bottom row\n  with the marker color.\n\nKey insight\n- The marker does not identify a color by value; it identifies a vertical drop\n  column, and only a structurally closed U shape can catch and contain the fill.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"singleton top-row marker pixel\",\n  \"path\": \"vertical drop down the marker column; a closed U-shaped wall container catches the drop when the marker column lies within its horizontal footprint, otherwise the path reaches the bottom edge\",\n  \"dst\": \"closed U-shaped container interior, or the bottom row if no closed container catches the drop\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"fill the caught container's background interior with the marker color; if uncaught, fill the whole bottom row\",\n  \"transform\": \"erase the original marker pixel and keep all wall pixels unchanged\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"753ea09b\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3109\nmechanism=0.3533\nlexical=0.0105\ncode_feature=0.5714\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:counter, object:line_segment, object:sprite, operation:count, output:same_size, relation:adjacent, relation:between, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/753ea09b.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/753ea09b.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nFill the small background compartments bounded by the long contour color.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid has one dominant background color and two foreground colors.\n- The more frequent foreground color forms long 8-connected contour fragments.\n- The other foreground color is a fixed distractor/obstacle color that partitions\n  the background but is never recolored.\n\nRule:\n- Split the background into 4-connected regions using all foreground pixels as\n  barriers.\n- Keep the two largest background regions as the outside of the contour drawing.\n- Recolor every other background region that touches a long contour component\n  to the contour color; leave all foreground pixels unchanged.\n\nKey insight:\nThe apparent area fill is exactly a component-level fill of bounded background\ncompartments, not a row-wise interpolation between individual contour pixels.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"4-connected background regions partitioned by long 8-connected contour-color components and obstacle-color pixels\",\n  \"transform\": \"recolor each non-exterior background region touching a long contour component to the contour color; keep the two largest background regions and all foreground pixels unchanged\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
